Travelling through what is now known as Kwa-Zulu Natal, Swaziland (Eswatini) and the Transkei between 1922 and the mid-1930s, Stern worked directly from the landscape and communities she encountered, creating charcoal studies, gouaches, sketches, paintings and sculpture.

